# --- B5: THE REACTIONS -----------------------------------------------------
# The line a character says when the world moves under them. The key is
# composed: dia.<character>.reaction.<thing>.<book|reality>. "book" is the
# reading they have just arrived at, not the one they left.

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "A giant!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a windmill again.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.reality"
msgstr "A mill."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a book.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.book"
msgstr "A book!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a rock again.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.reality"
msgstr "A rock."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "It's a mill."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a windmill again.
